```python
def selection_sort(arr):
    for i in range(len(arr)-1):
        min_idx = i
        for j in range(i+1, len(arr)):
            if arr[j] < arr[min_idx]:
                min_idx = j
        if min_idx != i:
            arr[i], arr[min_idx] = arr[min_idx], arr[i]
    return arr
```

This function takes an array as input and returns the sorted array. It uses a loop to iterate through the array, finding the minimum element in each iteration and swapping it with the element at the beginning of the array if necessary. The loop ends when all elements have been compared and swapped.

